  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 136 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nBy Friday, the upper ridge begins to expand back eastward. As this \noccurs, a stronger shortwave will move through the central Rockies \ninto the central and northern Plains and south winds return. As this \noccurs we will see temperatures respond back into the triple digits \nby the weekend with hot, dry and breezy conditions. The models do \nhint that this eastward expansion will be rather limited as the \nupper high continues to transition eastward and becomes centered \nover the southeast part of the CONUS. If this does in fact occur, it \nwould put the southern Plains into a southwest flow pattern and \nperhaps bring additional rain chances as we go into early September. \nUntil then, a continuation of hot and mainly dry conditions will \ncontinue.",
